Chart: A collection of files organized inside a specific directory structure that describes a related set of Kubernetes resources.

Values (values.yaml): The single place where configuration variables live. This is what you customize per environment without touching the underlying YAML blueprints.

Templates (templates/): Manifest blueprints that use the Go templating language ({{ .Values.variable }}) to inject values dynamically.

Release: A specific running instance of a chart in your cluster. You can install the same chart twice under different release names (e.g., my-app-dev and my-app-staging).

